The constructor of AbpApplicationBase is internal and takes three parameters, but the third parameter is an Action<AbpApplicationCreationOptions>? which can be null. The error suggests the constructor is not accessible from the test namespace. The test class must be in the same namespace and assembly or use InternalsVisibleTo attribute. Since I cannot change the assembly, I will create a derived class inside the Volo.Abp namespace in the test file to access the internal constructor and protected members. I will also add the using directive for Microsoft.Extensions.Configuration to get the GetValue extension method. I will retry with these fixes.

